DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonndd__wwaaiitt() function atomically blocks the current thread
     waiting on the condition variable specified by _c_o_n_d, and releases the mu‐
     tex specified by _m_u_t_e_x.  The waiting thread unblocks only after another
     thread calls pthread_cond_signal(3), or pthread_cond_broadcast(3) with
     the same condition variable, and the current thread reacquires the lock
     on _m_u_t_e_x.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, the pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonndd__wwaaiitt() function will return zero.  Other‐
     wise an error number will be returned to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The pptthhrreeaadd__ccoonndd__wwaaiitt() function will fail if:

     [EINVAL]           The value specified by _c_o_n_d or the value specified by
                        _m_u_t_e_x is invalid.

     [EPERM]            The specified _m_u_t_e_x was not locked by the calling
                        thread.

     [EOWNERDEAD]       The argument _m_u_t_e_x points to a robust mutex and the
                        process containing the previous owning thread termi‐
                        nated while holding the mutex lock.  The lock was
                        granted to the caller and it is up to the new owner to
                        make the state consistent.

     [ENOTRECOVERABLE]  The state protected by the _m_u_t_e_x is not recoverable.

